PS5: USB-C DisplayPort output (PSVR2) and GFX1013 fixes, ported to 7.3

ps5-linux-patches #57 by tertiumndatur (thanks rmuxnet), merged upstream on
7.2.3 (9bad84f), ported to our 7.3 tree (meower + our patches):
  - drivers/ps5/usbc_dp.c: USB-C controller policy (supported devices, NORMAL
    mode, state query, notifier; usbc_dp.aux / usbc_dp.hpd / lane budget params)
  - amdgpu_dm: a USB-C worker for native HPD, AUX receiver probing and DRM
    hotplug (7.3: in amdgpu_dm_irq.c, next to the HPD helpers it uses); the
    HDMI-bridge paths (HDR 4:2:2, audio/video mute, re-setup, link lock, the
    1440p fixup, mode limits, the standard mode set) stay off the USB-C link
  - DC/DCN201: ps5_usbc link state, AUX ignore-HPD gate, own link encoder
    funcs, DSC0
  - HDMI: the EDID is bound to the one bridge connector and stored under a
    lock, ICC message lengths validated (merged with our SCDC detection and
    re-arm; the log line stays "got real edid")
  - GFX1013: GFXOFF around compute idle, MMIO PASID TLB flushes instead of KIQ
  - spcie ICC teardown hardening, Salina xHCI 1 ms poll, threaded NAPI on the
    GbE, Bluetooth HIDP frames with MSG_DONTWAIT
PSVR2 needs userspace too: the patched Mesa for reprojection, PSVR2Toolkit.
Upstream tested on a fat console only.
